Soft immediates: a block whose own code the guest keeps patching reads
those operands from the code bytes at run time (M9 track,
docs/tracks/m9-tcg-aarch64.md).

The software renderers of the era write their inner loops as a template and
patch the operands into the instruction stream per span -- the texture base
as a disp32, the u/v steps as imm32, the carries as imm8, and, in the loop
that costs Moto Racer its tyre smoke, the RGB565 masks and shift counts of a
translucent span.  Patch 18 takes the rewrites that land on the value already
there (94 % of them); what is left really changes, and each one throws a
block away and pays a retranslation -- 31,000-36,500 a second in this game's
race, 30-36 MiB/s of host code, a third of the vCPU in translation.

A block at a physical address that four guest writes have thrown away is
translated again with its immediates and displacements emitted as host loads
of the guest's own code bytes instead of constants.  The guest's store is
then the update -- nothing is kept in step, and the block only has to survive
the write: it carries the list of byte ranges it reads that way, and a store
landing entirely inside them invalidates nothing.  Emitting the load is
correct on its own, and a field is registered only where the load is emitted,
so a use that kept its constant can never be left stale.  A block that is
thrown away four times *anyway* -- patched somewhere the code baked in --
gives up and goes back to constants.

Only the instructions whose emitter takes the immediate through gen_load and
nowhere else (ADD, OR, ADC, SBB, AND, SUB, XOR, MOV, which is also CMP and
TEST in the group-1 table); jump targets, shift counts, port numbers and the
SSE lane selectors stay constants because their emitters read
decode->immediate directly.  Little-endian hosts that allow unaligned loads
only, single-vCPU contexts only (CF_PARALLEL is left alone), first page of
the block only.

-accel tcg,soft-imm=off restores the old behaviour.  Test:
tools/smc-guest-test.py, whose 13 DOS cases now run in all four combinations
of soft-imm and smc-same-value and assert the path is reached (blocks
translated that way, writes absorbed) so it cannot pass by not testing it.
Moto Racer's race, on the driver's own frame counter: 41 -> 58 fps, the worst
5 s window 32 -> 45, invalidations 36,500/s -> 1/s.

